WEBVTT

00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:18.393
The netting structure has ruptured!

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.604
There's not a single
gauna response detected!

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:22.773
Is the hybrid safe?

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.234
Re-established connection
with hybrid Tsumugi! She's alive!

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:30.030
What the gauna did to me
was unspeakable.

00:00:30.906 --> 00:00:34.576
I will never let them do that
to my friends.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.663
Tsumugi has increased
her Heigus particle concentration!

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:39.373
<i>Damn it, stop this, Tsumugi!</i>

00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:43.210
Tsumugi! Listen to me!

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.170
No!

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.672
Heavy damage to Shinatose.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.883
Rapid rise in Gauna 550's
Heigus particle concentration!

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:51.468
Oh, no!

00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:56.181
Sidonia!

00:00:57.975 --> 00:01:02.145
Change in its trajectory at the point it
made contact with Tsumugi and Shinatose!

00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:04.481
Somebody... Tsumugi...

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:05.774
Hurry! Help!

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:09.736
It's Tsumugi!

00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:12.030
She needs help!

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:17.578
<i>Go forth and conquer!
<i>Let there be light!</i></i>

00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:26.878
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:27.671 --> 00:01:33.635
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:37.806
KNIGHTS OF SIDONIA

00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:47.733
<i>Our only haven is this fortress</i>

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:50.819
<i>Wandering among the stars</i>

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:54.072
<i>Where we tremble with impatience</i>

00:01:54.156 --> 00:01:56.491
<i>Between life and death</i>

00:01:56.825 --> 00:02:02.247
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:07.085
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:09.296 --> 00:02:15.218
<i>Those of us who have been led
<i>To gather here</i></i>

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:21.933
<i>Carry within ourselves the will to fight</i>

00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:25.562
<i>Our lives shine their brightest</i>

00:02:25.646 --> 00:02:28.065
<i>In the defense of love</i>

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:32.027
<i>We boldly enter the fray</i>

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.531
<i>The Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:46.458
HOPE

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:48.460
<i>Hybrid specimen maintenance team,</i>

00:02:48.627 --> 00:02:50.504
<i>report to Kunato Developments
<i>Arsenal Division</i></i>

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.631
<i>Special Culture Basin.</i>

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:56.468
<i>All medical teams,
<i>prepare to receive the injured pilots.</i></i>

00:02:57.094 --> 00:02:58.095
Sorry!

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:01.264
<i>Send the critically injured
<i>to the treatment centers.</i></i>

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:06.269
<i>Have the non-critically injured admitted
<i>to Medical Division 3 or Central Hospital.</i></i>

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:07.521
<i>All uninjured pilots...</i>

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:09.022
Izana...

00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:11.983
<i>please report to
<i>the waiting room for debriefing.</i></i>

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:18.281
How's Tsumugi?

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:22.911
She's fine. You don't need to worry.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:31.086
We need to hurry.

00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:32.921
Thank you!

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.224
-Kunato!
-Tanikaze...

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.518
How is Tsumugi?

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.857
She lost 90% of her body tissue.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.884
Don't worry.

00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:23.346
I promise I will restore Tsumugi
back to normal.

00:04:31.313 --> 00:04:34.691
<i>Roughly 50% of the gardes returning
<i>from the mission have been serviced</i></i>

00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:37.611
<i>and transferred to the standby hangar.</i>

00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:39.905
<i>This is Engine Maintenance,
<i>copy that.</i></i>

00:04:40.363 --> 00:04:43.742
Looks like we got saved
by that hybrid again.

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:48.497
We wouldn't still have a home to return to
if we were the only ones out there.

00:04:48.663 --> 00:04:50.624
Samari!

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.336
What?

00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:58.089
That really was a close one, huh?

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:01.510
I'm so glad that we all made it out!

00:05:04.012 --> 00:05:07.307
Tsuruuchi!

00:05:18.276 --> 00:05:21.947
Again with this. He hasn't changed a bit.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:25.492
That goes the same for you.
We just got back from that battle.

00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:28.245
Go easy on him.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:51.434
That's a pretty bold decision,
going with the mechanical prosthetic.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.354
My grandma recommended it to me...

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:58.358
since biological regeneration
would take too long.

00:06:00.151 --> 00:06:02.779
Don't worry,
you'll quickly get used to them.

00:06:03.488 --> 00:06:05.407
And they're so useful.

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:18.962
It's good to see you doing so well.

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:22.132
When will you get discharged?

00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:25.802
I'm ready to get discharged today.

00:06:26.344 --> 00:06:29.723
But anyway, how's Tsumugi, Nagate?

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:33.727
Oh, yeah...

00:06:41.026 --> 00:06:42.902
TO TSUMUGI
THANK YOU

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:48.033
DEAR TSUMUGI, THANK YOU FOR
PROTECTING SIDONIA. GET WELL SOON.

00:06:50.619 --> 00:06:53.747
-So many messages.
-Yeah.

00:07:04.007 --> 00:07:06.593
She's regenerated more
since last time.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:20.231
<i>We will be performing
<i>routine cleaning</i></i>

00:07:20.357 --> 00:07:22.776
<i>to the converter reactor tubes.</i>

00:07:24.486 --> 00:07:28.907
-I wish I could thank Tsumugi.
-Yeah.

00:07:30.659 --> 00:07:32.202
Tanikaze!

00:07:32.786 --> 00:07:35.205
I heard they changed our military rations!

00:07:35.497 --> 00:07:37.248
Let's go try them out!

00:07:40.794 --> 00:07:42.128
I'll pass this time.

00:07:42.337 --> 00:07:43.254
-What?
-What?

00:07:48.093 --> 00:07:49.844
Nagate...

00:07:56.726 --> 00:07:59.604
So, the colony ship
was attacked on its way back

00:07:59.771 --> 00:08:02.440
after dropping off the advance party?

00:08:02.816 --> 00:08:05.402
-Yes.
-Well, it's good to know that at least

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:08.113
there are some people
who made it to Planet 7 safely.

00:08:08.571 --> 00:08:09.614
Yes,

00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:13.535
but there's a gauna cluster
headed straight for the Lem Star System.

00:08:15.537 --> 00:08:17.455
Thank you for the meal.

00:08:18.123 --> 00:08:20.125
That's all you're eating?

00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:22.043
Good night.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.296
Good night.

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:29.634
Is he okay?

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:32.595
He seems really tired.

00:08:32.679 --> 00:08:35.056
I wonder if he's not sleeping well.

00:08:36.474 --> 00:08:40.145
Tanikaze isn't the type of person

00:08:40.228 --> 00:08:42.480
to say that he's tired
or not feeling well.

00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:45.233
It's a trait that I admire about him...

00:08:46.276 --> 00:08:49.195
but it does make you worry.

00:08:50.989 --> 00:08:55.035
I used to know someone
just like Nagate a long time ago,

00:08:55.243 --> 00:08:57.620
so I get a little worried too sometimes.

00:08:57.746 --> 00:09:01.124
Especially when I see him
taking too much upon himself.

00:09:01.666 --> 00:09:03.918
But I'm sure he'll be fine.

00:09:04.335 --> 00:09:06.921
Just give him space
and he'll cheer up eventually.

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:26.483
Nagate Tanikaze...

00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:31.237
Are you here to see Tsumugi again?

00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:34.991
Yes. Hello.

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:38.620
Tsumugi has been transferred
to the General Basin.

00:09:38.703 --> 00:09:40.747
Most of her ena has regenerated.

00:09:40.955 --> 00:09:44.167
All that's left is to wait for her
to regain consciousness.

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:47.921
Really? Thank you!

00:10:08.942 --> 00:10:10.360
Tsumugi!

00:10:14.155 --> 00:10:15.073
It moved!

00:10:23.081 --> 00:10:24.791
Yes!

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:28.545
She moved!

00:10:35.718 --> 00:10:38.388
Where are your manners?

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:56.489
What? Hoshijiro?

00:11:05.665 --> 00:11:07.417
Tanikaze.

00:11:11.921 --> 00:11:15.008
Hoshi... jiro...

00:11:16.885 --> 00:11:18.636
Tanikaze.

00:11:33.902 --> 00:11:35.236
Good morning.

00:11:36.571 --> 00:11:39.574
Good... morning?

00:11:40.158 --> 00:11:43.202
Did I fall asleep?

00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:46.706
You were sleeping very soundly.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.630
You're awake!

00:11:54.881 --> 00:11:56.507
Tsumugi...

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:57.800
Tanikaze?

00:11:57.926 --> 00:12:00.011
Oh, thank God!

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.103
Tsumugi!

00:12:09.354 --> 00:12:10.438
Izana!

00:12:10.605 --> 00:12:12.023
You're okay!

00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:13.775
Because of you!

00:12:14.025 --> 00:12:15.318
Thank you.

00:12:17.195 --> 00:12:18.613
Thank goodness!

00:12:19.781 --> 00:12:23.409
Look, I brought him along
because I heard you were awake.

00:12:23.826 --> 00:12:25.787
Oh, it's a cat!

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.915
May... may I touch it?

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.834
-Be gentle.
-Okay!

00:12:34.504 --> 00:12:37.131
It's so soft and cute!

00:12:40.635 --> 00:12:46.474
SITES OF SIDONIA
AUTOMATED FOOD STAND FLOOR

00:12:54.107 --> 00:12:57.777
Currently, the Gauna Cluster
is positioned between Sidonia and Lem,

00:12:58.027 --> 00:13:02.448
and we are in its blind spot
at the moment. We will begin decelerating

00:13:02.532 --> 00:13:04.951
in order to arrive
in the Lem Star System as planned.

00:13:06.911 --> 00:13:08.705
<i>Good. Stay vigilant.</i>

00:13:09.163 --> 00:13:10.665
<i>How is the hybrid?</i>

00:13:10.748 --> 00:13:12.417
Already regenerated.

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:16.754
She is currently standing by in a special
room built on the ship's outer hull.

00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:20.216
<i>I see. Good work.</i>

00:13:21.175 --> 00:13:23.261
GAUNA CLUSTER SIDONIA

00:13:23.344 --> 00:13:25.847
<i>Even if we included Tsumugi
<i>into our current firepower,</i></i>

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:28.599
<i>we don't have enough to go up
<i>against the gauna cluster.</i></i>

00:13:29.058 --> 00:13:32.854
<i>Does the captain have some other plan?</i>

00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:37.608
After that battle,

00:13:37.692 --> 00:13:41.738
the anti-hybrid movement
lost a lot of support.

00:13:41.904 --> 00:13:43.656
I would imagine so.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.992
How is the other thing coming along?

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:49.996
We're about to enter
the first phase of testing.

00:13:50.496 --> 00:13:54.917
Tell Professor Yure that I'm
looking forward to seeing her progress.

00:13:55.251 --> 00:13:56.961
Yes, captain.

00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:05.344
You can see outside?

00:14:05.803 --> 00:14:06.846
Yes!

00:14:06.929 --> 00:14:10.933
I guess this is slightly bigger
than the room you had before.

00:14:13.436 --> 00:14:17.607
I love reading, so I don't mind the size!

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:21.569
Tanikaze?

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:24.405
Oh, yeah. I was just thinking...

00:14:24.614 --> 00:14:28.826
this was a little far
from the residential district.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.537
Well, there's nothing I can do about that.

00:14:37.335 --> 00:14:38.628
What is it, Nagate?

00:14:38.753 --> 00:14:40.546
You've been awfully quiet.

00:14:40.713 --> 00:14:43.925
Tsumugi being out here
just reminded me

00:14:44.008 --> 00:14:46.677
what it was like when I was
living alone underground.

00:14:50.348 --> 00:14:55.937
Hey, let's ask Yuhata if we can bring
Tsumugi to the residential district!

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.522
That's a good idea!

00:14:57.605 --> 00:15:00.817
She might let us do it
if it's not for long!

00:15:02.568 --> 00:15:04.862
What kind of stupid question is that?

00:15:08.074 --> 00:15:09.617
Of course you can't!

00:15:09.992 --> 00:15:13.371
Even if you could,
the gravity is unstable right now!

00:15:13.454 --> 00:15:15.373
What would we do
if there was an accident?

00:15:15.957 --> 00:15:17.458
Now, stop being ridiculous!

00:15:17.792 --> 00:15:20.920
We... we're sorry.

00:15:42.108 --> 00:15:43.693
Hold on, wait!

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:46.404
Slow down, Nagate!

00:15:48.281 --> 00:15:50.950
Are you sure this is the right hole?

00:15:51.033 --> 00:15:51.951
Yeah.

00:15:52.326 --> 00:15:56.289
I checked to make sure
on the map I got from administration.

00:15:57.623 --> 00:16:01.169
Another dark passage?!

00:16:06.466 --> 00:16:09.010
You're bleeding! Sorry, Nagate!

00:16:09.093 --> 00:16:12.180
Oh, I'm fine.

00:16:12.263 --> 00:16:13.973
Let's keep going.

00:16:24.942 --> 00:16:27.528
Sidonia's front thrusters
have been opened!

00:16:27.612 --> 00:16:29.906
Pulling out the work team.

00:16:30.281 --> 00:16:34.076
Set course for Planet 9's trajectory.
Begin preparations to reverse thrusters!

00:16:34.285 --> 00:16:37.830
-Prepare to reverse thrusters!
-Issuing a gravity warning!

00:16:39.749 --> 00:16:44.086
<i>Sidonia will be reversing thrusters.</i>

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.048
<i>Please fasten your gravity belt
<i>to a safety railing</i></i>

00:16:47.131 --> 00:16:49.050
<i>and prepare for turbulence.</i>

00:16:49.717 --> 00:16:53.304
<i>Sidonia will be reversing thrusters.</i>

00:16:53.596 --> 00:16:56.599
<i>Please fasten your gravity
<i>belt to a safety railing</i></i>

00:16:56.682 --> 00:16:59.185
<i>and prepare for turbulence.</i>

00:17:03.022 --> 00:17:05.983
Nagate, did you just hear something?

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.861
What?

00:17:09.487 --> 00:17:10.780
We're almost there.

00:17:10.947 --> 00:17:12.198
Come on.

00:17:12.281 --> 00:17:13.616
Okay...

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:19.497
Ready to reverse thrusters!

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.999
Set ignition to Frontal Thrusters 1 and 2!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.001
Reverse thrusters!

00:17:40.017 --> 00:17:41.477
Wait, what's this vibration?

00:17:41.561 --> 00:17:43.563
Wait, wasn't today...

00:18:05.251 --> 00:18:07.461
We've stabilized.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:11.257
Restoring equilibrium
with the Gravity Field Generator.

00:18:16.804 --> 00:18:19.015
We're falling!

00:18:48.794 --> 00:18:51.964
Nagate, we made it out.

00:18:53.424 --> 00:18:54.800
Yeah.

00:19:19.867 --> 00:19:22.161
Found it! It's over here!

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.252
-Ready?
-Yeah.

00:20:12.586 --> 00:20:14.463
This is the residential tower?

00:20:14.547 --> 00:20:16.382
It's amazing.

00:20:16.841 --> 00:20:21.470
There must be so many people
living in those buildings.

00:20:21.554 --> 00:20:23.681
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:23.764 --> 00:20:25.474
Wow, look over there!

00:20:25.558 --> 00:20:26.809
There's so many people!

00:20:29.687 --> 00:20:34.150
There must be so many people
living so many different lives.

00:20:35.943 --> 00:20:38.154
How great would it be to shrink down

00:20:38.237 --> 00:20:42.074
to human size
so I could go around everywhere

00:20:42.158 --> 00:20:44.034
and be able to meet them all?

00:20:44.118 --> 00:20:47.538
There's nobody here
that doesn't know who you are, Tsumugi.

00:20:47.663 --> 00:20:50.499
They're all thankful.

00:20:50.791 --> 00:20:54.962
Thank you so much, both of you!

00:20:55.045 --> 00:20:56.547
I never thought

00:20:56.630 --> 00:21:02.845
I'd be able to see anything like this.

00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:25.659
Why's my stuff out in the hall?

00:21:27.703 --> 00:21:29.079
NEW CADETS MOVED IN TODAY.

00:21:29.205 --> 00:21:30.915
YOU HAD NOT PACKED.
WE SET YOUR THINGS OUT.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.500
Oh, right.

00:21:32.625 --> 00:21:36.045
I have to move out of the dorm.

00:21:50.184 --> 00:21:53.312
It's not funny, Grandma!

00:21:54.814 --> 00:21:56.315
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:56.398 --> 00:21:57.858
<i>But I'm glad.</i>

00:21:58.234 --> 00:22:01.821
<i>You're later than I thought you'd be,
<i>so I was getting worried.</i></i>

00:22:01.904 --> 00:22:05.783
<i>Oh, right, and your prosthetics
<i>will need adjusting, too.</i></i>

00:22:06.784 --> 00:22:09.411
Wait, hold on. I'm getting a call.

00:22:09.495 --> 00:22:11.914
<i>Okay. I'll hang up then.</i>

00:22:11.997 --> 00:22:14.124
Okay. Bye, Grandma.

00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:18.587
Izana?

00:22:18.963 --> 00:22:20.464
Nagate!

00:22:20.548 --> 00:22:22.299
What is it?

00:22:22.383 --> 00:22:24.802
<i>Sorry to spring this on you.</i>

00:22:24.885 --> 00:22:26.136
<i>Well...</i>

00:22:26.554 --> 00:22:29.098
<i>Could you put me up for the night?</i>

00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:40.401
What?!

00:22:40.776 --> 00:22:42.361
TO BE CONTINUED

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:50.828
<i>Oh, if this world must decay</i>

00:22:50.911 --> 00:22:54.582
<i>And I'm destined to give my life away</i>

00:22:54.665 --> 00:22:59.753
<i>What should I be living for?</i>

00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:05.676
<i>If I had never met you</i>

00:23:05.759 --> 00:23:09.346
<i>I would never have known</i>

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:15.352
<i>This pain that tears at my heart</i>

00:23:15.436 --> 00:23:17.771
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-Echoing there</i></i>

00:23:17.855 --> 00:23:19.857
<i>-Fortune
<i>-In the furthest reaches of the cosmos</i></i>

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:22.860
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Is this clumsy requiem</i></i>

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.237
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-And yet</i></i>

00:23:25.321 --> 00:23:27.156
<i>-Fortune
<i>-I'm still searching</i></i>

00:23:27.239 --> 00:23:30.576
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Within this uncertain reality</i></i>

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.661
<i>For you</i>

00:23:32.745 --> 00:23:36.373
<i>The joy of our finding each other</i>

00:23:36.457 --> 00:23:40.085
<i>The vanished warmth</i>

00:23:40.169 --> 00:23:43.797
<i>You should know that I remember it all</i>

00:23:43.881 --> 00:23:47.551
<i>Because I loved you</i>

00:23:47.635 --> 00:23:51.221
<i>The emotions that arise</i>

00:23:51.305 --> 00:23:54.850
<i>The scars left in my heart</i>

00:23:54.933 --> 00:23:59.271
<i>You should know that I'll carry them all</i>

00:23:59.355 --> 00:24:05.944
<i>As I walk this path</i>
